<Docs title="Sessions" description="Auto-save and resume conversations across sessions.">
  <h1>Sessions</h1>

  <h2>Auto-Save</h2>
  <p>
    Interactive sessions save a conversation snapshot on orderly exit. Resume restores recent
    canonical history and summarizes older messages for continuity; project memory remains a
    separate durable subsystem. A crash may leave durable turn-authority facts newer than the
    conversation snapshot.
  </p>

  <h2>Resume</h2>
  <pre><code># Resume the most recent session
{snippet("cli.resume")}

# Resume a specific session (prefix match)
{snippet("cli.resume_specific")}

# List saved sessions
{snippet("slash.sessions")}</code></pre>

  <h2>Session Contents</h2>
  <p>A saved session includes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Conversation messages and operator observations</li>
    <li>Intent and turn statistics</li>
    <li>Context decay window and compaction summary</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The snapshot does not promise an exact replay of prior model-visible context, provider state,
    project memory, persona, or tone.
  </p>
  <h2>Durable Turn Authority</h2>
  <p>
    Authority-backed interactive, ACP, daemon, Web/IPC, and <code>omegon run</code> paths record
    admitted prompts, FIFO queue order, active-turn identity, cancellation or revocation requests,
    and terminal outcomes in an adjacent authority stream. IPC and Web acceptance first means the
    runtime ingress received the command; clients observe durable queue state through subsequent
    runtime queue updates. A cancellation request leaves the turn busy while owned cleanup runs.
  </p>
  <p>
    Conversation JSON remains a compatibility snapshot. On restart, Omegon validates the
    authority stream, closes an interrupted active turn conservatively, and restores eligible
    queued prompts that reached durable admission. ACP withdraws orphaned queued requests when
    their client response channel was lost. Corrupt or unsupported authority data fails recovery
    instead of being repaired from conversation JSON. A maintenance resume deny fails before conversation
    loading; follow the <a href="/docs/recovery">recovery guide</a> to inspect it.
  </p>
  <!-- DIAGRAM:session-lifecycle | Timeline: session start -> durable turn facts plus conversation snapshot on orderly exit -> resume validates authority -> interrupted work closes conservatively -> recent history and summarized older context load. Show project memory as separate persistence. -->

  <h2>Disable Auto-Save</h2>
  <pre><code>{snippet("cli.no_session")}</code></pre>
  <p>
    Disables the conversation session snapshot and interactive authority sidecar for this run.
    Other configured subsystems, including project memory, logs, and audit records, may still
    persist data.
  </p>

  <h2>Headless Mode</h2>
  <p>
    For scripted/CI use, pass a prompt directly:
  </p>
  <pre><code># Execute a single prompt and exit
{snippet("cli.headless_prompt")}

# Read prompt from a file
{snippet("cli.headless_file")}

# Limit turns
{snippet("cli.headless_bounded")}</code></pre>

  <h2>Smoke Tests</h2>
  <pre><code>{snippet("cli.smoke")}</code></pre>
  <p>
    Runs 4 headless smoke tests through the LLM bridge: basic response, bash tool use,
    file read, and arithmetic validation. Useful for verifying provider connectivity and
    basic agent functionality after updates. 60-second timeout per test.
  </p>
</Docs>
